				\begin{document}$$\:\frac{\text{d}{N}_{C}\left(t\right)}{\text{d}t}={k}_{C}\left({T}_{ref}\right)\cdot\:{10}^{\frac{T\left(t\right)-{T}_{ref}}{{z{\prime\:}}_{C}}}\cdot\:\left(1-\text{e}\text{x}\text{p}\left({N}_{H}\left(t\right)-{N}_{C}\left(t\right)\right)\right)\:\text{w}\text{i}\text{t}\text{h}\:{N}_{C}\left(t=0\right)={N}_{C0}\:$$\end{document}

With parameters as described for Eqs. (1) and (2), and subscripts H and C referring to healthy and culturable cells, respectively. A Monte Carlo simulation was then conducted. For each iteration, a pseudo-random generator was used in MatLab to generate random parameter values for kH(Tref), z’H, kc(Tref), and z’C, using a normal distribution based on to the average and standard deviation of the respective parameter. Equations (3) and (4) were evaluated with these parameter values, using an average temperature profile for all model systems per microorganism. Then, SI was calculated as a function of time according to Eq. (5).5\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\:SI\left(t\right)=\frac{{N}_{C}\left(t\right)-{N}_{H}\left(t\right)}{{N}_{C}\left(t\right)}\cdot\:100\:\%$$\end{document}

The Time-averaged Injured Cells Coefficient (TICC) was calculated according to Eq. (6)27, using the calculated average SI curve.6\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
